    <text><list><item>Reversible-cause tests (blood count, metabolic panel, vitamin B12, folate, TSH) and one non-contrast brain MRI; syphilis and HIV testing only with risk factors or atypical features. Guideline: Practice parameter: diagnosis of dementia (an evidence-based review). Report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2001); Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for primary care (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Alzheimer&apos;s disease monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Behavioral neurology consultation to confirm the diagnosis, consider the type and biomarker testing, and advise on treatment and driving. Guideline: Practice parameter: diagnosis of dementia (an evidence-based review). Report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2001); Practice parameter update: evaluation and management of driving risk in dementia: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2010); The Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for specialty care (2025) [S]</item><item>Caregiver support: Zarit Burden Interview at diagnosis and every six to twelve months, education, adult day program and respite, and Alzheimer&apos;s Association support services. Guideline: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for primary care (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Alzheimer&apos;s disease monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Monitor on the CMID dementia schedule: medication review and neuropsychiatric screen at every visit; MoCA, ADL and IADL, CDR or FAST stage, depression screen, fall risk, driving, and advance care planning yearly; repeat tests or imaging only with a sudden change. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Alzheimer&apos;s disease monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Advance care planning while he can take part: name a health care agent and record his values and wishes. Guideline: Alzheimer&apos;s Association clinical practice guideline for the Diagnostic Evaluation, Testing, Counseling, and Disclosure of Suspected Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders (DETeCD-ADRD): Executive summary of recommendations for primary care (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Alzheimer&apos;s disease monographs (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

